     "assumptions": [
      "ASM-13 is used over ASM-5: 'cannot be delivered' means only an immediate error from the email sender, plus a missing billing email. All three drafts made this choice. Bounce webhooks (ASM-5, high risk) need confirming by the product owner before build. ASM-6's 'bounced' outcome is not used, so outcomes are 'sent' or 'failed'.",
